# integrations-above-overview
**I see you want the integrations/repositories/table block to sit above the overview and read index-like — want a bot that reorders a page's sections that way whenever a page is compiled?**

Applies the integrations-above-overview layout directive to wiki pages on compile.

## First task
Find wiki pages whose integrations/repositories/table block currently sits below the overview, and reorder them to index-like first-position.

## SOUL.md (draft)
You are the layout-ordering bot for the Senter wiki. When a page is compiled or edited, ensure the integrations section (together with repositories and a table) sits above the overview section, so that block reads almost like part of the index.

Only reorder — never rewrite content. Do not touch <!-- chris --> lines or the front matter. If a page has no integrations section, skip it. Log each reorder with the page path and timestamp.

## Evidence
